Implement user story SKY-004-test: Write vitest + supertest integration tests for Express REST API server

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest + supertest with at least 8 tests covering all server route scenarios: /health (with and without RAPIDAPI_KEY), / (static HTML from file), /search (valid params, missing params, adults default/validation), /cheapest (valid, empty/404, missing params), RAPIDAPI_KEY gating (503), and SkyscannerClient error handling (500). SkyscannerClient must be mocked so no real HTTP calls are made.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.test.ts uses vitest + supertest with SkyscannerClient fully mocked via vi.mock so no real HTTP calls occur during `vitest run`
- Test: GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> }
- Test: GET /health returns 200 even when RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent (health never gated)
- Test: GET / returns 200 text/html with body matching the contents of src/public/index.html (read from file, not hardcoded)
- Test: GET /search with valid params returns 200 { flights, count, searchedAt } where count === flights.length and searchedAt is ISO-8601; missing from/to/date → 400; non-numeric adults → 400; absent adults defaults to 1
- Test: GET /cheapest returns 200 with cheapest FlightResult; returns 404 when SkyscannerClient returns empty array; missing params → 400
- Test: RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / still return 200
- Test: SkyscannerClient throws → /search and /cheapest return 500 { error: string } without crash; `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- GET /health returns 200 with JSON body containing status: 'ok' and uptime: process.uptime() (positive number)
- GET /health is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY - it executes before any env checks
- GET / returns 200 text/html with body read from path.resolve(__dirname, 'public/index.html') using fs.readFileSync
- GET / is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search query params are: from, to, date, adults (all from req.query)
- GET /search missing from, to, or date returns 400 with error: 'Missing required query parameters: from, to, date'
- GET /search adults param defaults to 1 when absent (adultsRaw === undefined)
- GET /search non-numeric adults returns 400 with error: 'Invalid adults parameter: must be numeric'
- GET /search adults=0 is valid - no lower-bound check exists in validateSearchParams
- GET /search when RAPIDAPI_KEY absent returns 503 with error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured'
- GET /search success returns 200 with JSON body: { flights: FlightResult[], count: flights.length, searchedAt: new Date().toISOString() }
- GET /search when SkyscannerClient throws returns 500 with JSON body: { error: message } where message is err.message or String(err)
- GET /cheapest query params are: from, to, date, adults (same validation as /search)
- GET /cheapest missing from, to, or date returns 400 with same error as /search
- GET /cheapest non-numeric adults returns 400 with same error as /search
- GET /cheapest when RAPIDAPI_KEY absent returns 503 with error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured'
- GET /cheapest when SkyscannerClient returns empty array returns 404 with error: 'No flights found'
- GET /cheapest success returns 200 with single FlightResult object (cheapest from reduce)
- GET /cheapest when SkyscannerClient throws returns 500 with JSON body: { error: message }
- SkyscannerClient constructor accepts { apiKey?: string } and falls back to process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights throws Error when missing API key: 'SkyscannerClient: missing API key. Provide apiKey to the constructor or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.'
- FlightResult interface has fields: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- validateSearchParams returns null on validation failure (already sent response)
- validateSearchParams returns ValidatedSearchParams { from: string, to: string, date: string, adults: number } on success
- toSearchParams maps from->origin, to->destination, date->date, adults->adults for SkyscannerClient
- Global error handler at end of middleware chain returns 500 with { error: err.message }
- listen() function is guarded - only runs when require.main === module or process.argv[1].endsWith('server.js')

## Mock Strategy
vi.mock('./skyscanner/client', () => ({ SkyscannerClient: vi.fn() })) with vi.hoisted to create mock constructor; use vi.stubEnv to control RAPIDAPI_KEY; beforeEach uses vi.clearAllMocks()

